@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080

### Effective configuration, with no secrets
GET {{base}}/v1/config

### Preview chunking
POST {{base}}/v1/chunk
Content-Type: application/json

{"key":"markdown/example.md","markdown":"# Architecture\nThe application reads Markdown documents from RustFS and stores their dense and sparse embeddings in Qdrant for hybrid retrieval."}

### Index one object from the configured bucket (async)
POST {{base}}/v1/index
Content-Type: application/json

{"limit":1}

### Grounded answer or summary
POST {{base}}/v1/rag
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"Summarize the main findings in the indexed documents."}

### Run one benchmark query (async)
POST {{base}}/v1/benchmark
Content-Type: application/json

{"limit":1}

### Evaluate one generated benchmark result (async)
POST {{base}}/v1/eval
Content-Type: application/json

{"limit":1}

### Evaluate a supplied answer
POST {{base}}/v1/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json

{"question":"Which database stores embeddings?","answer":"Qdrant.","contexts":["Qdrant stores dense and sparse document embeddings."],"ground_truth":"Qdrant."}

### Analyze results and export the dashboard and failure files
POST {{base}}/v1/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{"export":true}
